Description: Fix Boost.Python test to request version-specific library
 Meson's Boost dependency resolver uses startswith() to match library names,
 which causes libboost_python313.so to be selected when only 'python3' is
 requested and the running Python is 3.14. The resulting extension module is
 compiled for the Python 3.14 ABI but linked against a 3.13 library, leading
 to a segfault at import time.
 .
 Work around this in the test by deriving the exact Boost Python module name
 from the detected Python installation (e.g. 'python314' for Python 3.14),
 and marking the dependency required:false so the test is skipped cleanly
 when no matching library is installed.
Author: Nadzeya Hutsko <nadzeya.hutsko@canonical.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson/issues/15596
Last-Update: 2026-03-04

diff --git a/test cases/frameworks/1 boost/meson.build b/test cases/frameworks/1 boost/meson.build
index 2e22cbf3..548ca0fb 100644
--- a/test cases/frameworks/1 boost/meson.build	
+++ b/test cases/frameworks/1 boost/meson.build	
@@ -37,7 +37,9 @@ else
 endif

 if(python3dep.found() and require_bp and not s)
-  bpython3dep = dependency('boost', static: s, modules : ['python3'])
+  _py3_ver = python3.language_version().split('.')
+  _py3_tag = _py3_ver[0] + _py3_ver[1]
+  bpython3dep = dependency('boost', static: s, modules : ['python' + _py3_tag], required: false, disabler: true)
 else
   python3dep = disabler()
   bpython3dep = disabler()
